    <briefdescription>
<para>Ebene-3 convergence-counting MetaVerdict assembler for the LDM. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>MetaVerdictBuilder combines Ebene-1 school verdicts, Ebene-2 cluster positions, legal-DB grounding, and mirror-school minority-dissent output into a single <computeroutput>MetaVerdict</computeroutput> that is EU AI Act Art. 13 compliant.</para>
<para>Convergence formula: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">convergence_score(v)<sp/>=<sp/>|{schools:<sp/>Ebene-1<sp/>verdict<sp/>==<sp/>v}|<sp/>/<sp/>N_active</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> where N_active = number of non-ABSTAIN schools in Ebene-1.</para>
<para>Edge cases:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>N_active == 0 (all ABSTAIN) → DISSENT MetaVerdict; EthicsErrorCode::LDM_ALL_ABSTAINED.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Legal-DB unavailable → <computeroutput>legal_grounding.grounding_available = false</computeroutput>; no exception.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<sect1 id="meta__verdict__builder_8h_1autotoc_md1_1s1"><sect2 id="meta__verdict__builder_8h_1autotoc_md1">
<title>Thread safety</title><para><computeroutput>buildMetaVerdict()</computeroutput> is stateless (all inputs are const references); it is safe to call from multiple threads simultaneously. <computeroutput>setLegalGrounding()</computeroutput> must be called before the first <computeroutput>buildMetaVerdict()</computeroutput> call (not thread-safe).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="since"><para>LDM-4 (Target: Q2 2027) </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
